WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.544 --> 00:00:16.888
Nina was quiet on the way to summer camp.

2
00:00:16.889 --> 00:00:20.001
"Don't be sad yet," said her mom.

3
00:00:20.002 --> 00:00:26.600
"You still have eight more hours of camp to enjoy.

4
00:00:26.601 --> 00:00:33.367
Go have fun, honey. Please!"

5
00:00:33.368 --> 00:00:39.754
On the blacktop Mr. Dunn was taping a large, square piece of mural paper to the ground.

6
00:00:39.755 --> 00:00:42.933
"Nina!" Ethan whispered loudly.

7
00:00:42.934 --> 00:00:46.730
He grabbed her arm and pulled her to the picnic table.

8
00:00:46.731 --> 00:00:55.968
"You have to sign Mr. Dunn's card."

9
00:00:55.969 --> 00:00:59.463
"Did you bring the watering can?" she asked.

10
00:00:59.464 --> 00:01:02.468
"Yep." Ethan giggled.

11
00:01:02.469 --> 00:01:05.396
"Izzie hid it in the girls' bathroom!"

12
00:01:05.397 --> 00:01:16.208
"All right. Time to start our final project," Mr. Dunn called.

13
00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:19.277
"Today we're making a quilt.

14
00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:24.701
It's like a quilt made of fabric, but ours will be made of paper.

15
00:01:24.702 --> 00:01:27.602
Everyone will design a square.

16
00:01:27.603 --> 00:01:31.905
Your square should show your favorite camp memory.

17
00:01:31.906 --> 00:01:40.630
But we're not really drawing our memories," Mr. Dunn said. "We're—"

18
00:01:40.631 --> 00:01:43.996
"Cutting paper!" Izzie cried.

19
00:01:43.997 --> 00:01:47.330
"Right, Izzie!" said Mr. Dunn.

20
00:01:47.331 --> 00:01:53.336
"We're going to cut shapes out of paper and glue them in our squares."

21
00:01:53.337 --> 00:02:00.590
They all headed to the picnic table to work.

22
00:02:00.591 --> 00:02:04.971
"What memory are you going to pick?" Izzie asked Nina.

23
00:02:04.972 --> 00:02:08.575
Nina sighed. "I don't know.

24
00:02:08.576 --> 00:02:11.322
I liked every day of camp!"

25
00:02:11.323 --> 00:02:16.767
"I'm picking the day we visited the animal shelter," Jason said.

26
00:02:16.768 --> 00:02:20.705
"And I got to see Lucy."

27
00:02:20.706 --> 00:02:23.906
"I want to pick the three-legged races.

28
00:02:23.907 --> 00:02:29.292
But that's going to be hard to show with paper shapes!" Bobby groaned.

29
00:02:29.293 --> 00:02:33.164
Izzie looked at Ethan's friendship bracelet and smiled.

30
00:02:33.165 --> 00:02:36.448
"I know what I'm going to choose."

31
00:02:36.449 --> 00:02:39.876
"What about you, Ethan?" Nina asked.

32
00:02:39.877 --> 00:02:44.189
"I liked when we made kites and flew them at the park," he said.

33
00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:51.540
"Okay, campers. Design your square in pencil first," Mr. Dunn said.

34
00:02:51.541 --> 00:02:54.965
"Then decide what color paper you need.

35
00:02:54.966 --> 00:03:02.430
If you're making a tree," Mr. Dunn went on, "you'll probably need brown paper for the trunk."

36
00:03:02.431 --> 00:03:06.899
"And green paper for the leaves," added Ethan.

37
00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.626
"Yep," said Mr. Dunn.

38
00:03:09.627 --> 00:03:15.615
"Does everyone understand what to do?"

39
00:03:15.616 --> 00:03:20.023
Nina understood how to cut the shapes and glue them on her square.

40
00:03:20.024 --> 00:03:23.349
She just couldn't choose the best day at camp.

41
00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:25.874
Was it when they made jam?

42
00:03:25.875 --> 00:03:29.049
Or the sea-breeze wind chimes?

43
00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:32.834
She watched her friends working.

44
00:03:32.835 --> 00:03:38.979
At last she got an idea.

45
00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:42.869
Everyone quietly cut and glued paper.

46
00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:45.713
Before they knew it, they were done.

47
00:03:45.714 --> 00:03:51.717
"Now let's put our squares together on the mural paper!" said Mr. Dunn.

48
00:03:51.718 --> 00:03:55.498
"We'll arrange them in time order."

49
00:03:55.499 --> 00:03:57.369
"Oh my gosh, Nina!"

50
00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:00.934
Izzie gasped when she saw Nina's.

51
00:04:00.935 --> 00:04:05.520
"Nina, that's beautiful!" Mr. Dunn exclaimed.

52
00:04:05.521 --> 00:04:12.469
Nina had carefully cut out tiny people working on even tinier colorful quilt squares.

53
00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:17.050
"I like yours too," Nina told Mr. Dunn.

54
00:04:17.051 --> 00:04:22.478
His square showed the water balloon toss from the first day of camp.

55
00:04:22.479 --> 00:04:27.623
"That's when I first met you guys." Mr. Dunn smiled.

56
00:04:27.624 --> 00:04:33.059
"Definitely the best day of the summer."

57
00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:42.416
At the end of the day, all the parents admired the quilt.

58
00:04:42.417 --> 00:04:46.778
The kids gave Mr. Dunn his card and the watering can.

59
00:04:46.779 --> 00:04:51.570
Everyone thought Mr. Dunn looked a little teary.

60
00:04:51.571 --> 00:04:55.615
"Were you okay today, honey?" Nina's mom asked.

61
00:04:55.616 --> 00:05:00.502
Nina pointed at her square.

62
00:05:00.503 --> 00:05:12.227
"I had the best last day ever!"
